# Sin, Spira's Punishment (CR 701.13, 707.2, 111.1, 110.4a, 700.7): Bot1's graveyard holds two Islands (discarded to Faithless
# Looting) and the Black Lotus sacrificed to cast Sin (Faithless Looting itself is no permanent card); Bot2's holds a Black Lotus
# (and later a discarded Island), never touched. When Sin enters the dice pick an Island first - a land, so the process repeats -
# then the Black Lotus: nonland, so it ends, with a tapped Island token and a tapped Black Lotus token and one Island left. When Sin
# attacks on turn 5 the die picks the last Island, a land that repeats the process on a graveyard with no permanent card left -
# nothing more - while Bot2's cards are still there.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Faithless Looting
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Sin, Spira's Punishment
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Island x19

[Dice]
1; 2; 1

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Island; Island)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sin, Spira's Punishment.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Graveyard = Faithless Looting; Island
? Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Tapped = true
? Bot2.Graveyard = Black Lotus
[T5 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Sin, Spira's Punishment)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Faithless Looting
Bot2.Graveyard = Island; Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 8
